i","address":"krzysztof.kozlowski@oss.qualcomm.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"Julius Werner","address":"jwerner@chromium.org"},{"name":"Sean Rhodes","address":"sean@starlabs.systems"},{"name":"","address":"chrome-platform@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"Corentin Chary","address":"corentin.chary@gmail.com"},{"name":"Luke D. Jones","address":"luke@ljones.dev"},{"name":"Denis Benato","address":"denis.benato@linux.dev"},{"name":"Hans de Goede","address":"hansg@kernel.org"},{"name":"Ilpo Järvinen","address":"ilpo.jarvinen@linux.intel.com"},{"name":"Prasanth Ksr","address":"prasanth.ksr@dell.com"},{"name":"Jorge Lopez","address":"jorge.lopez2@hp.com"},{"name":"Mark Pearson","address":"mpearson-lenovo@squebb.ca"},{"name":"Derek J. Clark","address":"derekjohn.clark@gmail.com"},{"name":"Joshua Grisham","address":"josh@joshuagrisham.com"},{"name":"","address":"platform-driver-x86@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"Dell.Client.Kernel@dell.com"},{"name":"Florian Fainelli","address":"florian.fainelli@broadcom.com"},{"name":"Huacai Chen","address":"chenhuacai@kernel.org"},{"name":"Michael S. Tsirkin","address":"mst@redhat.com"},{"name":"Chen-Yu Tsai","address":"wenst@chromium.org"},{"name":"Tzung-Bi Shih","address":"tzungbi@kernel.org"},{"name":"Brian Norris","address":"briannorris@chromium.org"},{"name":"Thomas Zimmermann","address":"tzimmermann@suse.de"},{"name":"Javier Martinez Canillas","address":"javierm@redhat.com"},{"name":"Maarten Lankhorst","address":"maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com"},{"name":"Maxime Ripard","address":"mripard@kernel.org"},{"name":"David Airlie","address":"airlied@gmail.com"},{"name":"Simona Vetter","address":"simona@ffwll.ch"},{"name":"Bjorn Andersson","address":"andersson@kernel.org"},{"name":"Geert Uytterhoeven","address":"geert@linux-m68k.org"},{"name":"Dmitry Baryshkov","address":"dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"Arnd Bergmann","address":"arnd@arndb.de"},{"name":"Eric Biggers","address":"ebiggers@kernel.org"},{"name":"Luca Weiss","address":"luca.weiss@fairphone.com"},{"name":"Michal Simek","address":"michal.simek@amd.com"},{"name":"Sven Peter","address":"sven@kernel.org"},{"name":"Uwe Kleine-König (The Capable Hub)","address":"u.kleine-koenig@baylibre.com"},{"name":"Bjorn Helgaas","address":"bhelgaas@google.com"},{"name":"Danilo Krummrich","address":"dakr@kernel.org"},{"name":"Takashi Sakamoto","address":"o-takashi@sakamocchi.jp"},{"name":"Titouan Ameline de Cadeville","address":"titouan.ameline@gmail.com"},{"name":"Kees Cook","address":"kees@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org"},{"name":"Oliver Lin","address":"oliver@liuxiaozhen.dev"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-12T19:47:48.000Z","iso":"2026-08-12T19:47:48.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v11 3/4] firmware: Rename google firmware directory to coreboot","mailingLists":[{"id":"platform-driver-x86.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"platform-driver-x86.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"I do not consider marketing or pure \"I do not like this name\" as valid"},{"depth":1,"text":"reasons, because this is developer string (or kernel/distro"},{"depth":1,"text":"configurator) not end-user visible thing. And for us, the developers,"},{"depth":1,"text":"this marketing does not matter."}],"lineCount":4,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I'm not sure I'd agree that naming doesn't matter for developers? The\nstyle guide has an entire section about choosing good names for C\nsymbols, I don't think Kconfig symbols are fundamentally different in\nthat regard; they're still strings developers read to find and make\nsense of things, and leaving something with the wrong name makes it\nharder for the reading developer to find and understand it. (This\nisn't about \"marketing\", btw, Google the company doesn't care whether\nthis driver is called GOOGLE or COREBOOT. I care as a kernel developer\nthat this driver has been mostly used for something else than what it\nwas originally labeled for for a long while and it's high time that we\ncorrect that to avoid confusing people.)"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Anyway, defconfig change must be separate because it goes via different"},{"depth":1,"text":"tree, unless this is non bisectable. Keeping it here initially confused"},{"depth":1,"text":"me into thinking you are actually breaking use cases (which you are not)."}],"lineCount":3,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fair enough. So Sean, could you maybe split this out into this patch\nwhich does everything (the renaming and adding of transitional\nsymbols) except for the arm64 defconfig change, and then the defconfig\nchange as a separate patch at the end of the series so that it can go\nthrough a different tree?"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"c8e4a3d3-a96d-4fd1-85a6-881e68385c83@oss.qualcomm.com"}},"rootIds":["CAODwPW__tskkkqSREHFAf9iG17oYfG5Li-1kh0y8pX=z0W_31A@mail.gmail.com"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["CAODwPW__tskkkqSREHFAf9iG17oYfG5Li-1kh0y8pX=z0W_31A@mail.gmail.com"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}